  "description": "The canonical-form declarations of an IDL vocabulary (Phase 539): a member's ALIASES (retired spellings a decoder accepts and normalises to the canonical name, the canonical spelling winning when both are present, otherwise the first alias in declared order), an enum case's aliases (lenient wire strings that decode to the case and re-encode as its canonical string), a member's PRESENCE condition (`whenPresent` / `whenAbsent` an Optional sibling, or `whenEquals` a sibling's scalar value, an absent OmitDefault sibling holding its default; a member whose condition fails is absent from the canonical form, so a decoder drops it UNREAD, whatever its value, ill-typed included, and it decodes as its optionality's absence), and an empty-map or JSON default literal (omitted at its default, compared by canonical bytes). `vocabulary` is the fixture's idl.json; each vector reads `document` (a node over that vocabulary) and expects `expected`, the canonical bytes the reference decodes and re-encodes it to, or `refusal`, the decode `code` and the `path` to the fault (each segment a member's key or an index), computed by calling the pinned kit. A path names the document AS WRITTEN (Phase 723): a fault inside a member read under an alias is located at the alias, whether the member is a kind's, a record's or a union case's, and at any depth beneath it; where both spellings are present the canonical one is read, so the path names it; and a missing member's path ends at the absent key, its canonical spelling.",
